# Droppings of TaleWorlds' Workshop uploader when run from the repo root
steam_appid.txt
steam_workshop_uploader.txt

# The voices themselves are NOT tracked, on purpose.
#
# Everything currently in module\Voices is cloned either from Bannerlord's own dialogue actors or
# from real people (Sibylla, Max). Deploying them locally is fine and intended; publishing them is
# not, and a git history is forever - which makes an accidental "commit all" from a GUI the one
# mistake that cannot be taken back. package.ps1 already refuses to zip them; this refuses to
# record them.
#
# The folder shape and its README ARE tracked, so the layout ships and stays documented.
#
# WHEN THERE ARE VOICES WE MAY GENUINELY SHIP (CC0-sourced - see module\Voices\README.txt), delete
# these four lines. That deletion is meant to be a deliberate moment, not a default.
module/Voices/**/voice.json
module/Voices/**/embedding.json
module/Voices/**/icl-prompt.json
module/Voices/**/reference.wav
